  </div>

  <div class="highlight-box">
    <h4>Key Takeaway for Investors</h4>
    <p>An investment of <strong>$10,000</strong> in AXP at the start of the dataset (June 1972 at ${fmt(first_close, 2)}/share) would have grown to approximately <strong>${fmt(10000 * (last_close / first_close), 0)}</strong> by March 2026 (at ${fmt(last_close, 2)}/share), excluding dividends. The stock has compounded at <strong>{pct(cagr_pct, 2)}</strong> annually, turning every dollar into <strong>${fmt(last_close / first_close, 0)}</strong> over 53.8 years. AXP's journey reflects the resilience of a premier financial franchise through multiple economic cycles, from oil crises and market crashes to the digital payments revolution. The stock currently trades at ${fmt(latest_close, 2)} ({pct(pct_from_ath, 1)} from its all-time high of ${fmt(ath, 2)} on {ath_date}).</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ═══════════ PRICE TREND ANALYSIS ═══════════ -->
<section id="price-trend-analysis">
  <h2>Long-Term Price Trend Analysis</h2>

  <div class="chart-container">
    <div id="chart-price" class="chart"></div>
  </div>

  <h3>Bull & Bear Phases (≥20% Declines)</h3>
  <p style="margin-bottom: 14px; font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--text-light);">
    The table below identifies major bear phases where AXP declined 20% or more from a prior peak,
    along with the duration and recovery time of each episode.
  </p>

  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Period</th><th>Peak</th><th>Trough</th><th>Decline</th><th>Approx. Duration</th><th>Recovery Date</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
"""

for p in phases:
    dur = (p["end"] - p["start"]).days
    rec_str = p["recovery_date"].strftime("%b %Y") if p["recovery_date"] else "Not yet recovered"
    html += f"""
      <tr>
        <td>{p['start'].strftime('%b %Y')} – {p['end'].strftime('%b %Y')}</td>
        <td>${fmt(p['peak'], 2)}</td>
        <td>${fmt(p['trough'], 2)}</td>
        <td class="negative">-{pct(p['decline'], 1)}</td>
        <td>{dur} days</td>
        <td>{rec_str}</td>
      </tr>"""

html += """
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h3>Long-Term Growth: Sub-Period CAGR</h3>
  <p style="margin-bottom: 14px; font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--text-light);">
    Annualized returns over key multi-decade holding periods.
  </p>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Period</th><th>Start Price</th><th>End Price</th><th>Years</th><th>CAGR</th><th>Total Return</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
"""

sub_periods = [
    ("1972–2026 (Full)", rows[0], rows[-1]),
]
# Add decade-level periods
decades_list = ["1970s", "1980s", "1990s", "2000s", "2010s", "2020s"]
for dn in decades_list:
    if dn in decade_stats:
        ds = decade_stats[dn]
        sub_periods.append((dn, None, None))
        # We'll fill from decade_stats

for sp_name, sp_start, sp_end in sub_periods:
    if sp_start and sp_end:
        sy = (sp_end["date"] - sp_start["date"]).days / 365.25
        scagr = ((sp_end["close"] / sp_start["close"]) ** (1/sy) - 1) * 100
        sret = (sp_end["close"] / sp_start["close"] - 1) * 100
        html += f"""
        <tr>
          <td><strong>{sp_name}</strong></td>
          <td>${fmt(sp_start['close'], 2)}</td>
          <td>${fmt(sp_end['close'], 2)}</td>
          <td>{sy:.1f}</td>
          <td class="positive">{pct(scagr, 2)}</td>
          <td class="positive">{pct(sret, 0)}</td>
        </tr>"""

for dn in decades_list:
    if dn in decade_stats:
        ds = decade_stats[dn]
        cl = "positive" if ds["total_return"] >= 0 else "negative"
        html += f"""
        <tr>
          <td><strong>{dn}</strong></td>
          <td>${fmt(ds['start_price'], 2)}</td>
          <td>${fmt(ds['end_price'], 2)}</td>
          <td>~10</td>
          <td class="{cl}">{pct(ds['cagr'], 2)}</td>
          <td class="{cl}">{pct(ds['total_return'], 0)}</td>
        </tr>"""

html += f"""
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <div class="highlight-box" style="margin-top: 16px;">
    <h4>Record Levels</h4>
    <p><strong>All-Time High:</strong> ${fmt(ath, 2)} on {ath_date} &nbsp;|&nbsp;
    <strong>All-Time Low:</strong> ${fmt(all_time_low, 2)} on {atl_date} &nbsp;|&nbsp;
    <strong>Current ({latest_date_str}):</strong> ${fmt(latest_close, 2)}</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ═══════════ VOLATILITY & RISK ═══════════ -->
<section id="volatility-risk">
  <h2>Volatility & Risk Assessment</h2>

  <div class="chart-container">
    <div id="chart-drawdown" class="chart"></div>
  </div>

  <div class="two-col">
    <div>
      <h3>Risk Metrics</h3>
      <table>
        <tr><td>Annualized Volatility</td><td><strong>{pct(annualized_vol_pct, 1)}</strong></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Daily Volatility</td><td><strong>{pct(daily_vol * 100, 3)}</strong></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Maximum Drawdown</td><td><strong class="negative">-{pct(max_drawdown_pct, 1)}</strong></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Worst Single-Day Drop</td><td><strong class="negative">-{pct(min(daily_returns) * 100, 1)}</strong></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Best Single-Day Gain</td><td><strong class="positive">+{pct(max(daily_returns) * 100, 1)}</strong></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Positive Day Ratio</td><td><strong>{pct(sum(1 for r in daily_returns if r > 0) / len(daily_returns) * 100, 1)}</strong></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Sharpe Ratio (approx.)</td><td><strong>{fmt((cagr - 0.03) / max(annualized_vol, 0.001), 2)}</strong></td></tr>
      </table>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3>Major Crash Episodes</h3>
"""

for cd in crash_details:
    html += f"""
      <div class="phase-card" style="margin-bottom: 8px;">
        <div class="phase-title">{cd['name']}</div>
        <div class="phase-dates">{cd['start']} → {cd['end']}</div>
        <div class="phase-data">
          Peak: <strong>${fmt(cd['peak'], 2)}</strong> →
          Trough: <strong>${fmt(cd['trough'], 2)}</strong> &nbsp;
          <span class="negative">-{pct(cd['drawdown'], 1)}</span>
        </div>
      </div>"""

html += """
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ═══════════ VOLUME ANALYSIS ═══════════ -->
<section id="volume-analysis">
  <h2>Trading Volume Analysis</h2>

  <div class="chart-container">
    <div id="chart-volume" class="chart"></div>
  </div>

  <p style="font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--text-light); margin-bottom: 16px;">
    Trading volume data is sparse in the dataset's early years (1970s–early 1980s show near-zero volume).
    Reliable volume data emerges from the mid-1980s onward, reflecting both improved data collection
    and structural growth in equity market participation.
  </p>

  <div class="highlight-box">
    <h4>Volume Observations</h4>
    <p>AXP's trading volume has grown substantially over the decades, with average daily volume in the 2020s
    reaching several million shares. Notable volume spikes coincide with major market events: the 2008–2009
    financial crisis, the COVID-19 crash of 2020, and earnings announcements. The secular increase in volume
    reflects both AXP's growth in market capitalization and the broader electronification of equity markets.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ═══════════ DIVIDEND HISTORY & STOCK SPLITS ═══════════ -->
<section id="dividends-splits">
  <h2>Dividend History & Stock Splits</h2>

  <div class="chart-container">
    <div id="chart-dividends" class="chart"></div>
  </div>

  <div class="two-col">
