        <td class="{cl_c}">{pct(ds['cagr'], 2)}</td>
        <td>{pct(ds['volatility'], 1)}</td>
        <td class="negative">-{pct(ds['max_drawdown'], 1)}</td>
        <td>${fmt(ds['dividends'], 2)}</td>
        <td>{ds['trading_days']:,}</td>
      </tr>"""

html += """
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <div class="highlight-box">
    <h4>Decade Context</h4>
    <p><strong>1970s:</strong> Oil crises and stagflation dominated, yet AXP compounded positively as the credit card industry took hold.<br>
    <strong>1980s:</strong> Strong bull market amid disinflation and financial services deregulation. Black Monday (1987) was a sharp but brief interruption.<br>
    <strong>1990s:</strong> One of the strongest decades for U.S. equities. AXP benefited from the consumer credit boom and the rise of electronic payments.<br>
    <strong>2000s:</strong> The "lost decade" for equities. AXP was hit by the dot-com bust and especially the 2008 financial crisis — its worst drawdown on record.<br>
    <strong>2010s:</strong> A powerful recovery decade. AXP transformed into a digital-first payments network with strong total returns and growing dividends.<br>
    <strong>2020s:</strong> Shaped by COVID-19's sharp crash and rapid recovery, sustained by fiscal stimulus and the shift to digital payments.</p>
  </div>
</section>

